<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Clear any "lurking" Commands and all Readies, set NO MODE]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OFF-SCAN (EnableIn is False) STATUS
============================================================
If this device is OFF-SCAN (rung is false or EnableIn is false in FBD), then:

Handle "NO MODE" Selection using the standard P_Mode AOI (EnableInFalse Routine, false scan required!).

NOTE:  IN ORDER TO AVOID USING AN "AFI" (which will generate a routine verify warning),
THIS RUNG USES AN XIC of Cfg_PCmdClear, followed by an XIO of the SAME BIT
to ensure P_Mode is SCANNED FALSE ("NO MODE").

THIS IS NOT DEAD CODE AND MUST APPEAR EXACTLY AS SHOWN FOR PROPER OPERATION!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)XIO(Cfg_PCmdClear)P_Mode(Mode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[First-Come First-Served Ownership Arbitration still needs to happen, even when device is disabled.
If a requestor supplies a non-zero Owner ID and the current owner is NONE (zero),
Ownership is assigned to the requesting ID.  When that requestor sets the Owner ID back
to zero, Ownership is relinquished back to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(PSet_Owner,0) ,EQU(Val_Owner,0) ]MOV(PSet_Owner,Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Program Commands are cleared if they are set as "Edge" triggered
(cleared by this object as received).
(Lurking Acknowledge Commands are left to perform their action.)

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added PCmd_Bump  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)[OTU(PCmd_StartTot) OTU(PCmd_StopTot) OTU(PCmd_StartFlow) OTU(PCmd_StopFlow) ,OTU(PCmd_Bump) OTU(PCmd_ClearTot) OTU(PCmd_CheckTol) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Operator Commands are cleared, as well as Program Reset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(OCmd_StartTot) OTU(OCmd_StopTot) OTU(OCmd_StartFlow) OTU(OCmd_StopFlow) OTU(OCmd_ClearTot) ,OTU(OCmd_CheckTol) OTU(OCmd_Bump) OTU(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Since we're not processing Operator Commands or Settings, we're not READY for any of them either!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Rdy_StartTot) OTU(Rdy_StopTot) OTU(Rdy_StartFlow) OTU(Rdy_StopFlow) OTU(Rdy_ClearTot) ,OTU(Rdy_CheckTol) OTU(Rdy_Bump) OTU(Rdy_Reset) OTU(Rdy_ResetAckAll) ,OTU(Rdy_SP) OTU(Rdy_DribPre) OTU(Rdy_Tol) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Show the Dosing as Disabled and Not Ready, not Available.
Clear remaining Status bits.
Show the enumerated command as NONE.
Show the enumerated status as DISABLED.
Show the enumerated fault status as NONE.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTL(Sts_NotRdy) OTL(Nrdy_NoMode) OTU(Nrdy_CfgErr) OTU(Nrdy_EqpFault) OTU(Nrdy_PVBad) ,OTU(Sts_Available) OTU(Sts_MaintByp) ,OTU(Sts_TotRunning) OTU(Sts_FlowStarting) OTU(Sts_DribbleStarting) OTU(Sts_FlowStopping) ,CLR(Val_Cmd) MOV(33,Val_Sts) CLR(Val_Fault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
EQUIPMENT FEEDBACK PROCESSING
============================================================
If the equipment is being simulated or provides no feedback,
loop back the outputs  to provide "fake" feedback.

If the equipment is NOT being simulated and it HAS feedback,
use the state of the run feedback input and dribble feedback
input to show the current equipment state.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Fdbk) ,[XIO(Inp_Sim) XIC(Cfg_HasEqpFdbk) XIO(Inp_RunFdbk) XIO(Inp_DribbleFdbk) XIC(Inp_StopFdbk) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) ,XIO(Cfg_HasEqpFdbk) ] MOV(1,Wrk_Fdbk) OTE(Sts_FlowStopped) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) XIC(Cfg_HasEqpFdbk) [XIC(Inp_RunFdbk) XIO(Inp_DribbleFdbk) XIO(Inp_StopFdbk) MOV(2,Wrk_Fdbk) OTE(Sts_FlowRunning) ,XIO(Inp_RunFdbk) XIC(Inp_DribbleFdbk) XIO(Inp_StopFdbk) MOV(3,Wrk_Fdbk) OTE(Sts_FlowDribble) ] ,MOV(Wrk_Fdbk,Val_Fdbk) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
VALUES PROCESSING
============================================================
In preparation for calculating Values (Rate, Quantity, Remaining),
this determines the time since the previous scan (used for
rate, totalizing functions).using a non-stop TON timer.
When we get here, we read the accumulator (in milliseconds, so
divide by 1000.0 to get seconds), then clear the accumulator.  Next scan the accumulator will have
incremented up to the number of milliseconds since last scan.  (Works for scan times up to 2 million seconds.....)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(2147483647,Wrk_ScanT.PRE)TON(Wrk_ScanT,?,?)DIV(Wrk_ScanT.ACC,1000.0,Wrk_ScanTime)CLR(Wrk_ScanT.ACC);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CHECK INPUTS FOR INFINITE / NOT A NUMBER
============================================================
This rung determines whether the Quantity PV Input is +/-Infinity or +/- NotANumber,
and whether the Rate PV Input is +/- Infinity or +/- NotANumber.

If the Quantity Input PV is an exception, if the quantity is not calculated from rate, the bad quantity is being used,
and if the rate IS calculated from the bad quantity, the rate is bad.

If the Rate Input PV is an exception, if the rate is not calculated from quantity, the bad rate is being used,
and if the quantity IS calculated from the bad rate, the quantity is bad.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Wrk_QtyInfNaN)OTU(Wrk_RateInfNaN)[COP(Inp_QtyPV,Wrk_QtyInpDINT,1) MEQ(Wrk_QtyInpDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000) [XIO(Cfg_CalcQty) OTL(Wrk_QtyInfNaN) MOV(Inp_QtyPV,Val_Qty) ,XIC(Cfg_CalcRate) OTL(Wrk_RateInfNaN) MOV(Inp_QtyPV,Val_Rate) ] ,COP(Inp_RatePV,Wrk_RateInpDINT,1) MEQ(Wrk_RateInpDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000) [XIO(Cfg_CalcRate) OTL(Wrk_RateInfNaN) MOV(Inp_RatePV,Val_Rate) ,XIC(Cfg_CalcQty) OTL(Wrk_QtyInfNaN) MOV(Inp_RatePV,Val_Qty) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[These two rungs select whether to use a Simulated flowmeter rate
or the actual flowmeter rate.

In simulation, start with the rate at zero.  But if Flow is Running, use the full
simulation rate, and if Flow is Dribbling, use the dribble simulation rate.

NOTE:    simulation ALWAYS uses the configured simulation rates to determine rate
and total, regardless of the configuration of Cfg_CalcRate and Cfg_CalcQty.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Inp_Sim)CLR(Wrk_Rate);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Rate is not simulated, not calculated from changes in Quantity, and is
not Infinite or Not a Number, use it for the Rate in remaining calculations.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)XIO(Cfg_CalcRate)XIO(Wrk_RateInfNaN)MOV(Inp_RatePV,Wrk_Rate);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copy the current input to a "Previous Quantity" rung for use in the
difference calculations next TRUE scan.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(Inp_QtyPV,Wrk_PrevQty);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung handles the case where the Quantity input is used directly, for example, when
the flowmeter has a totalizer on board and we are using its total.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Cfg_CalcQty)XIO(Inp_Sim)LEQ(Cfg_Rollover,0.0)XIO(Wrk_QtyInfNaN)[GRT(Cfg_CountsPerEU,0.0) DIV(Inp_QtyPV,Cfg_CountsPerEU,Val_Qty) ,LEQ(Cfg_CountsPerEU,0.0) MOV(Inp_QtyPV,Val_Qty) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Rate is to be calculated based on change in quantity, take the change in Quantity
calculated above, divide by scan time, adjust for per second, per minute, per hour (etc.),
and adjust for conversion of quantity units to rate units (e.g. GPM to BBL/Day...).
Then filter (1st order) based on the entered time constant.

If the rate is NOT to be calculated, just pass through the input Rate PV to the Val_Rate.

If the input was +/-Infinity or Not a Number and it becomes a valid number,
initialize the filter to start from the first valid value.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RateInfNaN)[XIC(Cfg_CalcRate) CLR(Wrk_Rate) ,GRT(Cfg_RateFiltTC,0.0) CPT(Wrk_Alpha,1.0/(1.0+Wrk_ScanTime/Cfg_RateFiltTC)) ,LEQ(Cfg_RateFiltTC,0.0) CLR(Wrk_Alpha) ,ONS(Wrk_ValidONS) MOV(Wrk_Rate,Wrk_FiltRate) ,CPT(Wrk_FiltRate,(Wrk_Alpha*Wrk_FiltRate)+((1.0-Wrk_Alpha)*Wrk_Rate)) MOV(Wrk_FiltRate,Val_Rate) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the quantity Remaining to Deliver and the Percent Complete.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Val_Remain)CLR(Val_PctComplete);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
EQUIPMENT FAULT DETERMINATION
============================================================
If the input being used to calculate the Quantity (total) is BAD, the Quantity is BAD.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for use with Source/Quality enumerations below.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Inp_RatePVBad) XIC(Cfg_CalcQty) ,XIC(Inp_QtyPVBad) XIO(Cfg_CalcQty) ,XIC(Wrk_QtyInfNaN) ]XIO(Inp_Sim)OTE(Sts_QtyBad);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the input being used to calculate the Rate (flow) is BAD, the Rate is BAD (failed).

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for use with Source/Quality enumerations below.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Inp_QtyPVBad) XIC(Cfg_CalcRate) ,XIC(Inp_RatePVBad) XIO(Cfg_CalcRate) ,XIC(Wrk_RateInfNaN) ]XIO(Inp_Sim)OTE(Sts_RateBad);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the input being used to calculate the Quantity (total) is UNCERTAIN, the Quantity is UNCERTAIN.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for use with Source/Quality enumerations below.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Inp_RatePVUncertain) XIC(Cfg_CalcQty) ,XIC(Inp_QtyPVUncertain) XIO(Cfg_CalcQty) ]XIO(Inp_Sim)OTE(Sts_QtyUncertain);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the input being used to calculate the Rate (flow) is UNCERTAIN, the Rate is UNCERTAIN.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for use with Source/Quality enumerations below.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Inp_RatePVUncertain) XIO(Cfg_CalcRate) ,XIC(Inp_QtyPVUncertain) XIC(Cfg_CalcRate) ]XIO(Inp_Sim)OTE(Sts_RateUncertain);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Flow is stopped on EnableIn False.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Out_RunFlow)OTU(Out_DribbleFlow)OTL(Out_StopFlow);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENUMERATED STATUS VALUES
============================================================
Source and Quality (Srcq) for Val_InpPV
Start with the Srcq from the Input Channel object if it's available.
Otherwise, start based on bad/uncertain input bits.

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Cfg_CalcQty) MOV(Inp_RatePVSrcQ,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIO(Cfg_CalcQty) MOV(Inp_QtyPVSrcQ,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIO(Cfg_HasEqpFdbk) LES(Wrk_SrcQ,2) MOV(2,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Cfg_CalcQty) [XIC(Sts_RateUncertain) MOV(16,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Sts_RateBad) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Wrk_RateInfNaN) MOV(32,Wrk_SrcQ) ] ,XIO(Cfg_CalcQty) [XIC(Sts_QtyUncertain) MOV(16,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Sts_QtyBad) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Wrk_QtyInfNaN) MOV(32,Wrk_SrcQ) ] ,XIC(Err_EU) MOV(35,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(10,Wrk_SrcQ) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ,SrcQ_IO) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality (SrcQ) for Val (primary value)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(20,SrcQ);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear the Alarms and the Notify Status, and show the Alarms Inhibited breadcrumb.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Alm_OverTol) OTU(Alm_UnderTol) OTU(Alm_EqpFault) OTU(Alm_ZeroFault) ,OTU(Sts_OverTol) OTU(Sts_UnderTol) OTU(Sts_EqpFault) OTU(Sts_ZeroFault) ,OTL(Sts_AlmInh) CLR(Val_Notify) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Normal Scan: control / monitor Dosing with Flowmeter]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.
============================================================
P_DoseFM:  PROCESS -- FLOWMETER DOSING
============================================================
Revision 3.1-02 Release  2014-09-30.  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V1.x and V2.x Revision History archived.
V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib.  Added settle time before tolerance check;
added PCmd_Bump.  Using P_Alarm V3.0, P_Mode V3.0.  Removed Err_Keep.
Added Cfg_HasChanObjRate, Cfg_HasChanObjQty.
V3.0-01  2013-07-30:  Modified Parameter descriptions only.
V3.0-02  2013-09-03:  Modified Parameter descriptions only.
V3.0-03  2013-10-30:  Corrected Parameter descriptions and default
configuration values for alarms only.
V3.0-04  2014-01-22:   Corrected Settle Time preset check,
Cfg_SetTrack default value.
V3.1-00  2014-07-08:  Modified to use P_Alarm, P_Mode V3.1; added
Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_Xxxxx), source/quality values (SrcQ).
Modified to consistently use alias tag names.
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Exposed Bump, Fault, Settle timers ACC/PRE (read-only).
Corrections to Nrdy_ resets. Using P_Alarm, P_Mode V3.1-01.
Modified simulated equipment feedback.
V3.1-02  2014-09-30:  Unchanged, but using P_Alarm V3.1-02.
============================================================
This Instruction monitors a flowmeter which provides flow rate (AI),
quantity pulses (e.g., 1756-CFM / -HSC), or rate and total (fieldbus),
and provides:

*  Optional integration (totalizing) of analog flow to a Quantity
*  Optional differentiation of pulse count or quantity to a flow Rate
*  Commands to Start, Stop and Clear the Quantity (total)
*  Outputs to run and clear an external totalizer (say, on fieldbus flowmeter)
*  Commands to Start and Stop Flow for a dosing
*  Optional switching to a slow delivery (dribble) when approaching setpoint
*  Stopping flow just before reaching setpoint using a Preact value
*  Optional automatic adjustment of the preact value to fine tune the stop point
*  Commands to check if the delivered quantity is within user-specified tolerances and alarm if not
*  Program and Operator Settings for Setpoint, Preact, Dribble Quantity, High and Low Tolerances
*  Equipment Failure Alarm on sensor failure (stops totalizer, stops flow),
Equipment Feedback failure or other controlled equipment failure (stops flow)
*  Zero failure alarm if quantity does not zero when totalizer is cleared
*  Configurable Low Flow Cutoff to account for zero error on analog flowmeters
*  Conversion of flow units to alternate quantity units (e.g., GPM to Barrels)
*  Monitoring of optional equipment status feedback
*  Simulation using a provided simulated Rate and simulated Dribble Rate

Modes are provided by a P_Mode AOI instance.
Alarms are provided by P_Alarm AOI instances.
Modes of operation: Operator, Program, Maintenance
============================================================
SHOW LOCAL STRINGS
============================================================
The STRINGs containing the text associated with each instance of this
instruction cannot be Input or Output Parameters, because STRINGs are not
 'atomic' types. (Inputs and Outputs must be SINT, INT, DINT, REAL, or BOOL.)

In order to make it easier to find and configure these STRINGs, this rung
was added.  THE JMP (and the LBL on the following rung)
MUST NOT BE REMOVED!!!

To view the STRINGs, go to the instruction instance (in LD or FBD), RIGHT-click
to bring up the context menu and select "Open Instruction Logic".
This rung will appear with the STRING values for the selected instance.
You may double-click the STRING values here to modify them as well.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[JMP(SkipText)CONCAT(Cfg_Desc,Cfg_Label,Cfg_Tag)LOWER(Cfg_QtyEU,Cfg_RateEU)LOWER(Inf_Lib,Inf_Type);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
MODE PROCESSING
============================================================
This rung handles received Mode Inputs and Commands:

NOTE:  All Commands for Mode, Alarm are aliased directly to the
corresponding Commands in the contained P_Mode and P_Alarm AOIs.

This object does NOT have the following Modes:
Hand
Override]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[LBL(SkipText)OTU(Mode.Inp_Hand)OTU(Mode.Inp_Ovrd)P_Mode(Mode);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung handles simple First-Come First-Served Ownership Arbitration.
If a requestor supplies a non-zero Owner ID and the current owner is NONE (zero),
Ownership is assigned to the requesting ID.  When that requestor sets the Owner ID back
to zero, Ownership is relinquished back to NONE.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(PSet_Owner,0) ,EQU(Val_Owner,0) ]MOV(PSet_Owner,Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CONFIGURATION PROCESSING
============================================================
If the device is configured to not HAVE device feedback input (engineer),
it cannot be USE the feedback for fail checking (maintenance).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Cfg_HasEqpFdbk)OTU(Cfg_UseEqpFdbk);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Maintenance Bypass function is active, display the Maintenance Bypass
Indicator (triangle symbol) on the graphic symbol.  Bypass functions are:
*  Controlled Equipment HAS feedback designated by engineer, but
maintenance has selected to NOT USE equipment feedback]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_HasEqpFdbk)XIO(Cfg_UseEqpFdbk)OTE(Sts_MaintByp);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Cfg_AutoAdjPct: Limit the Preact Auto Adjustment Percentage to a value between 0.0 and 100.0 percent.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[LES(Cfg_AutoAdjPct,0.0) CLR(Cfg_AutoAdjPct) ,GRT(Cfg_AutoAdjPct,100.0) MOV(100.0,Cfg_AutoAdjPct) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
MODE PROCESSING: "ASPECT" OWNERSHIP
============================================================
Using the Mode determined above, and the Cfg_OperKeep and
Cfg_ProgKeep bits, determine who (Prog or Oper) "owns"
each of the Device's "aspects":
Start/Stop (.0), Setpoint (.1), Dribble/Preact (.2),
and Over/Under Delivery Tolerances (.3).

The bits within Cfg_OperKeep and Cfg_ProgKeep determine which "aspects"
(sub-functions of this AOI) are retained by the Operator in Program Mode,
or by the Program in Operator Mode (respectively).

All aspects (functions) may be "kept" (basically locking the Operator/Program Mode
selection, rendering it moot --  you get to explain how it works to your operators!!!),
but it is NOT allowed to have any given function retained by BOTH Operator and
Program.  This rung ensures that no function is "kept" by both Oper and Prog.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Cfg_OperKeep.0) ONS(Wrk_OperKeep0ONS) OTU(Cfg_ProgKeep.0) ,XIC(Cfg_OperKeep.1) ONS(Wrk_OperKeep1ONS) OTU(Cfg_ProgKeep.1) ,XIC(Cfg_OperKeep.2) ONS(Wrk_OperKeep2ONS) OTU(Cfg_ProgKeep.2) ,XIC(Cfg_OperKeep.3) ONS(Wrk_OperKeep3ONS) OTU(Cfg_ProgKeep.3) ,XIC(Cfg_ProgKeep.0) ONS(Wrk_ProgKeep0ONS) OTU(Cfg_OperKeep.0) ,XIC(Cfg_ProgKeep.1) ONS(Wrk_ProgKeep1ONS) OTU(Cfg_OperKeep.1) ,XIC(Cfg_ProgKeep.2) ONS(Wrk_ProgKeep2ONS) OTU(Cfg_OperKeep.2) ,XIC(Cfg_ProgKeep.3) ONS(Wrk_ProgKeep3ONS) OTU(Cfg_OperKeep.3) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung handles the reports of all Error (Bad Configuration) Status.

Individual bits are provided for various status:
Invalid Engineering Units Scaling configs
Invalid Rate calculation configs
Invalid Limit configs
Invalid Simulation configs
Invalid Timer configs (determined in Configuration section above)
Invalid Alarm configs
Invalid Cfg_OperKeep, Cfg_ProgKeep

Then a summary Error Status is provided, simply an OR of the individual bits.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Settle Timer  #####
#####  V3.0-04  2014-01-20:  Fixed Settle Timer preset sign check.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[LEQ(Cfg_CountsPerEU,0.0) ,LEQ(Cfg_EUQtyMult,0.0) ,LES(Cfg_Rollover,0.0) ] OTE(Err_EU) ,[LES(Cfg_RateFiltTC,0.0) ,LEQ(Cfg_RateTime,0.0) ] OTE(Err_Rate) ,LES(Cfg_LoRateCutoff,0.0) OTE(Err_Cutoff) ,LEQ(Cfg_MaxQty,0.0) OTE(Err_Limit) ,[LEQ(Cfg_SimDribbleRate,0.0) ,LEQ(Cfg_SimRate,0.0) ] OTE(Err_Sim) ,[MUL(Cfg_SettleT,1000,Wrk_SettleT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_SettleT.PRE.31) CLR(Wrk_SettleT.PRE) ,MUL(Cfg_BumpT,1000.0,Wrk_BumpT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_BumpT.PRE.31) CLR(Wrk_BumpT.PRE) ,MUL(Cfg_ClearPulseT,1000,Wrk_ClearPulseT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_ClearPulseT.PRE.31) CLR(Wrk_ClearPulseT.PRE) ,MUL(Cfg_FaultT,1000,Wrk_FaultT.PRE) XIC(Wrk_FaultT.PRE.31) CLR(Wrk_FaultT.PRE) ] OTE(Err_Timer) ,[XIC(OverTol.Sts_Err) ,XIC(UnderTol.Sts_Err) ,XIC(ZeroFault.Sts_Err) ,XIC(EqpFault.Sts_Err) ] OTE(Err_Alarm) ]OTE(Sts_Err);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
EQUIPMENT FEEDBACK PROCESSING
============================================================
If the equipment is being simulated or provides no feedback,
loop back the outputs  to provide "fake" feedback.

If the equipment is NOT being simulated and it HAS feedback,
use the state of the run feedback input and dribble feedback
input to show the current equipment state.

#####  V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Modified simulated equipment feedback.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Fdbk) ,[XIO(Cfg_UseEqpFdbk) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) ] [XIO(Out_RunFlow) XIO(Out_DribbleFlow) MOV(1,Wrk_Fdbk) ,XIC(Out_RunFlow) XIO(Out_DribbleFlow) MOV(2,Wrk_Fdbk) ,XIO(Out_RunFlow) XIC(Out_DribbleFlow) MOV(3,Wrk_Fdbk) ] ,XIO(Inp_Sim) XIC(Cfg_UseEqpFdbk) [XIO(Inp_RunFdbk) XIO(Inp_DribbleFdbk) XIC(Inp_StopFdbk) MOV(1,Wrk_Fdbk) ,XIC(Inp_RunFdbk) XIO(Inp_DribbleFdbk) XIO(Inp_StopFdbk) MOV(2,Wrk_Fdbk) ,XIO(Inp_RunFdbk) XIC(Inp_DribbleFdbk) XIO(Inp_StopFdbk) MOV(3,Wrk_Fdbk) ] ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(4,Val_Fdbk) ,XIO(Inp_Sim) MOV(Wrk_Fdbk,Val_Fdbk) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SETTINGS PROCESSING
============================================================
The following two rungs check the Settings (Program Settings here, Operator
Settings below) to be sure they "make sense".  They are limited unconditionally
in case Setting Tracking is disabled.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(PSet_SP,Cfg_MaxQty) MOV(Cfg_MaxQty,PSet_SP) ,LES(PSet_SP,0.0) CLR(PSet_SP) ,GRT(PSet_Preact,PSet_SP) MOV(PSet_SP,PSet_Preact) ,LES(PSet_Preact,0.0) CLR(PSet_Preact) ,GRT(PSet_DribbleQty,PSet_SP) MOV(PSet_SP,PSet_DribbleQty) ,LES(PSet_DribbleQty,0.0) CLR(PSet_DribbleQty) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(OSet_SP,Cfg_MaxQty) MOV(Cfg_MaxQty,OSet_SP) ,LES(OSet_SP,0.0) CLR(OSet_SP) ,GRT(OSet_Preact,OSet_SP) MOV(OSet_SP,OSet_Preact) ,LES(OSet_Preact,0.0) CLR(OSet_Preact) ,GRT(OSet_DribbleQty,OSet_SP) MOV(OSet_SP,OSet_DribbleQty) ,LES(OSet_DribbleQty,0.0) CLR(OSet_DribbleQty) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SETTINGS PROCESSING
============================================================
This rung handles received Settings:

When the Mode is Program, use the Program Settings for the Quantities,
Tolerances, etc., and (if so enabled) copy the Program Settings to the Operator Settings
for bumpless transition from Program to Operator.

When the Mode is Operator, use the Operator Settings for the Quantities,
Tolerances, etc., and (if so enabled) copy the Operator Settings to the Program Settings
for bumpless transition from Operator to Program.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(Sts_Prog) XIO(Cfg_OperKeep.1) ,XIC(Sts_Oper) XIC(Cfg_ProgKeep.1) ] MOV(PSet_SP,Val_SP) ,[XIC(Sts_Prog) XIO(Cfg_OperKeep.2) ,XIC(Sts_Oper) XIC(Cfg_ProgKeep.2) ] MOV(PSet_DribbleQty,Val_DribbleQty) MOV(PSet_Preact,Val_Preact) ,[XIC(Sts_Prog) XIO(Cfg_OperKeep.3) ,XIC(Sts_Oper) XIC(Cfg_ProgKeep.3) ] MOV(PSet_TolHi,Val_TolHi) MOV(PSet_TolLo,Val_TolLo) ,[XIC(Sts_Oper) XIO(Cfg_ProgKeep.1) ,XIC(Sts_Prog) XIC(Cfg_OperKeep.1) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] MOV(OSet_SP,Val_SP) ,[XIC(Sts_Oper) XIO(Cfg_ProgKeep.2) ,XIC(Sts_Prog) XIC(Cfg_OperKeep.2) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] MOV(OSet_DribbleQty,Val_DribbleQty) MOV(OSet_Preact,Val_Preact) ,[XIC(Sts_Oper) XIO(Cfg_ProgKeep.3) ,XIC(Sts_Prog) XIC(Cfg_OperKeep.3) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] MOV(OSet_TolHi,Val_TolHi) MOV(OSet_TolLo,Val_TolLo) ,XIC(Cfg_SetTrack) [MOV(Val_SP,OSet_SP) MOV(Val_DribbleQty,OSet_DribbleQty) MOV(Val_Preact,OSet_Preact) MOV(Val_TolHi,OSet_TolHi) MOV(Val_TolLo,OSet_TolLo) ,MOV(Val_SP,PSet_SP) MOV(Val_DribbleQty,PSet_DribbleQty) MOV(Val_Preact,PSet_Preact) MOV(Val_TolHi,PSet_TolHi) MOV(Val_TolLo,PSet_TolLo) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
CHECK INPUTS FOR INFINITE / NOT A NUMBER
============================================================
This rung determines whether the Quantity PV Input is +/-Infinity or +/- NotANumber,
and whether the Rate PV Input is +/- Infinity or +/- NotANumber.

If the Quantity Input PV is an exception, if the quantity is not calculated from rate, the bad quantity is being used,
and if the rate IS calculated from the bad quantity, the rate is bad.

If the Rate Input PV is an exception, if the rate is not calculated from quantity, the bad rate is being used,
and if the quantity IS calculated from the bad rate, the quantity is bad.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Wrk_QtyInfNaN)OTU(Wrk_RateInfNaN)[COP(Inp_QtyPV,Wrk_QtyInpDINT,1) MEQ(Wrk_QtyInpDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000) [XIO(Cfg_CalcQty) OTL(Wrk_QtyInfNaN) MOV(Inp_QtyPV,Val_Qty) ,XIC(Cfg_CalcRate) OTL(Wrk_RateInfNaN) MOV(Inp_QtyPV,Val_Rate) ] ,COP(Inp_RatePV,Wrk_RateInpDINT,1) MEQ(Wrk_RateInpDINT,16#7F80_0000,16#7F80_0000) [XIO(Cfg_CalcRate) OTL(Wrk_RateInfNaN) MOV(Inp_RatePV,Val_Rate) ,XIC(Cfg_CalcQty) OTL(Wrk_QtyInfNaN) MOV(Inp_RatePV,Val_Qty) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM RESET COMMAND HANDLING
============================================================
This rung handles the Alarm Reset Input and Commands
and the "Reset and Ack All" Operator Command.

This rung processes received Reset Commands from:

1.  The Operator via HMI Operator Command, or
2.  Higher-level strategies via Program Command
3.  Pushbuttons or other block via Input

and forwards the Reset to ALL Alarms and latched Shed conditions.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-08-29:  Corrections to Nrdy_ resets.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_Reset) ,XIC(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) [OTL(PCmd_OverTolAck) ,OTL(PCmd_UnderTolAck) ,OTL(PCmd_ZeroFaultAck) ,OTL(PCmd_EqpFaultAck) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Reset) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ,NOP() ] ,XIC(Inp_Reset) ][OTL(OverTol.PCmd_Reset) OTL(UnderTol.PCmd_Reset) OTL(ZeroFault.PCmd_Reset) OTL(EqpFault.PCmd_Reset) ,OTU(Wrk_OverTol) OTU(Wrk_UnderTol) OTU(Wrk_ZeroFault) ,XIO(Sts_EqpFault) OTU(Nrdy_EqpFault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
COMMAND PROCESSING
============================================================
The rungs below handle received Commands.
Clear Val_Cmd in preparation.

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Wrk_Cmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[OCmd_ClearTot / PCmd_ClearTot: Clear Totalizer Total]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_ClearTot) OTU(OCmd_ClearTot) [XIC(Sts_Oper) XIO(Cfg_ProgKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Prog) XIC(Cfg_OperKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_ClearTot) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_ClearTot) ,NOP() ] [XIC(Sts_Prog) XIO(Cfg_OperKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Oper) XIC(Cfg_ProgKeep.0) ] ]XIO(Wrk_RunFlow)XIO(Wrk_BumpFlow)[OTL(Wrk_ClearTot) OTU(Wrk_BumpNoAdj) OTU(Wrk_ZeroFault) ,OTU(Wrk_OverTol) OTU(Wrk_UnderTol) OTU(Wrk_InTol) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[OCmd_StartTot / PCmd_StartTot: Start Totalizer]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_StartTot) OTU(OCmd_StartTot) [XIC(Sts_Oper) XIO(Cfg_ProgKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Prog) XIC(Cfg_OperKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_StartTot) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_StartTot) ,NOP() ] [XIC(Sts_Prog) XIO(Cfg_OperKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Oper) XIC(Cfg_ProgKeep.0) ] ]OTL(Wrk_RunTot)MOV(2,Wrk_Cmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[OCmd_StopTot / PCmd_StopTot: Stop Totalizer]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_StopTot) OTU(OCmd_StopTot) [XIC(Sts_Oper) XIO(Cfg_ProgKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Prog) XIC(Cfg_OperKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_StopTot) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_StopTot) ,NOP() ] [XIC(Sts_Prog) XIO(Cfg_OperKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Oper) XIC(Cfg_ProgKeep.0) ] ,[XIC(Inp_RatePVBad) XIC(Cfg_CalcQty) ,XIC(Inp_QtyPVBad) XIO(Cfg_CalcQty) ,XIC(Wrk_QtyInfNaN) ] XIO(Inp_Sim) ]OTU(Wrk_RunTot)MOV(7,Wrk_Cmd);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[OCmd_StartFlow / PCmd_StartFlow: Start Dosing (flow)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_StartFlow) OTU(OCmd_StartFlow) [XIC(Sts_Oper) XIO(Cfg_ProgKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Prog) XIC(Cfg_OperKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_StartFlow) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_StartFlow) ,NOP() ] [XIC(Sts_Prog) XIO(Cfg_OperKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Oper) XIC(Cfg_ProgKeep.0) ] ]XIO(Wrk_BumpFlow)[OTL(Wrk_RunFlow) OTU(Wrk_ClearTot) OTU(Wrk_ZeroFault) ,OTU(Wrk_OverTol) OTU(Wrk_UnderTol) OTU(Wrk_InTol) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[BUMP FLOW:  Run / Dribble Flow to make up for under-tolerance.
If the Bump Timer Preset is NONZERO, bump for a fixed time ("Bump Time").
If the Bump Timer Preset is ZERO, bump until the bump command bit is turned
off (works like JOG on a drive).

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added PCmd_Bump  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_Bump) [NEQ(Wrk_BumpT.PRE,0) OTU(OCmd_Bump) ,NOP() ] [XIC(Sts_Oper) XIO(Cfg_ProgKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Prog) XIC(Cfg_OperKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_Bump) [NEQ(Wrk_BumpT.PRE,0) OTU(PCmd_Bump) ,NOP() ] [XIC(Sts_Prog) XIO(Cfg_OperKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Oper) XIC(Cfg_ProgKeep.0) ] ]XIO(Wrk_RunFlow)[OTL(Wrk_BumpFlow) OTL(Wrk_BumpNoAdj) ,OTU(Wrk_ClearTot) OTU(Wrk_ZeroFault) ,OTU(Wrk_OverTol) OTU(Wrk_UnderTol) OTU(Wrk_InTol) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If a Bump Flow is running and the Bump Timer expires (non-zero preset, bump for time)
or the Bump Command is cleared (zero preset, bump like a JOG), stop bump flow.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_BumpFlow)[TON(Wrk_BumpT,?,?) ,[GRT(Wrk_BumpT.PRE,0) XIC(Wrk_BumpT.DN) ,EQU(Wrk_BumpT.PRE,0) XIO(OCmd_Bump) ] OTU(Wrk_BumpFlow) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[OCmd_StopFlow / PCmd_StopFlow: Stop Dosing (flow)

If the input being used to calculate the Quantity (total) is BAD,
the Quantity is BAD (failed).  If the Quantity is bad or
the controlled equipment sheds, or there is a
configuration error, we stop the delivery.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_StopFlow) OTU(OCmd_StopFlow) [XIC(Sts_Oper) XIO(Cfg_ProgKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Prog) XIC(Cfg_OperKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_StopFlow) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_StopFlow) ,NOP() ] [XIC(Sts_Prog) XIO(Cfg_OperKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Oper) XIC(Cfg_ProgKeep.0) ] ,XIC(Sts_Err) ,[XIC(Inp_RatePVBad) XIC(Cfg_CalcQty) ,XIC(Inp_QtyPVBad) XIO(Cfg_CalcQty) ,XIC(Wrk_QtyInfNaN) ] XIO(Inp_Sim) OTE(Sts_QtyBad) ,XIC(Inp_CtrldEqpFault) XIO(Inp_Sim) XIC(Cfg_ShedOnEqpFault) ,XIC(Nrdy_EqpFault) ]OTU(Wrk_BumpFlow)OTU(Wrk_RunFlow);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[OCmd_CheckTol / PCmd_CheckTol: Check Total Quantity
against Setpoint and Tolerances: Is delivery in tolerance?

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Settle Timer  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OCmd_CheckTol) OTU(OCmd_CheckTol) [XIC(Sts_Oper) XIO(Cfg_ProgKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Prog) XIC(Cfg_OperKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ] ,XIC(PCmd_CheckTol) [XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear) OTU(PCmd_CheckTol) ,NOP() ] [XIC(Sts_Prog) XIO(Cfg_OperKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Oper) XIC(Cfg_ProgKeep.0) ] ]XIO(Sts_Cleared)XIC(Wrk_SettleT.DN)[OTU(Wrk_OverTol) OTU(Wrk_UnderTol) OTU(Wrk_InTol) ,CMP(Val_Qty>(Val_SP+Val_TolHi)) OTL(Wrk_OverTol) ,CMP(Val_Qty<(Val_SP-Val_TolLo)) OTL(Wrk_UnderTol) ,XIO(Wrk_OverTol) XIO(Wrk_UnderTol) OTL(Wrk_InTol) ,XIC(Cfg_AutoAdjPreact) XIO(Wrk_BumpNoAdj) OTL(Wrk_BumpNoAdj) XIC(Wrk_InTol) [CPT(Val_Preact,Val_Preact-((Val_SP-Val_Qty)*Cfg_AutoAdjPct/100.0)) ,MOV(Val_Preact,PSet_Preact) MOV(Val_Preact,OSet_Preact) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
VALUES PROCESSING
============================================================
In preparation for calculating Values (Rate, Quantity, Remaining),
this determines the time since the previous scan (used for
rate, totalizing functions).using a non-stop TON timer.
When we get here, we read the accumulator (in milliseconds, so
divide by 1000.0 to get seconds), then clear the accumulator.  Next scan the accumulator will have
incremented up to the number of milliseconds since last scan.  (Works for scan times up to 2 million seconds.....)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(2147483647,Wrk_ScanT.PRE)TON(Wrk_ScanT,?,?)DIV(Wrk_ScanT.ACC,1000.0,Wrk_ScanTime)CLR(Wrk_ScanT.ACC);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[These two rungs select whether to use a Simulated flowmeter rate
or the actual flowmeter rate.

In simulation, start with the rate at zero.  But if Flow is Running, use the full
simulation rate, and if Flow is Dribbling, use the dribble simulation rate.

NOTE:    simulation ALWAYS uses the configured simulation rates to determine rate
and total, regardless of the configuration of Cfg_CalcRate and Cfg_CalcQty.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Inp_Sim)[CLR(Wrk_Rate) ,XIC(Sts_FlowRunning) MOV(Cfg_SimRate,Wrk_Rate) ,XIC(Sts_FlowDribble) MOV(Cfg_SimDribbleRate,Wrk_Rate) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Rate is not simulated, not calculated from changes in Quantity, and is
not Infinite or Not a Number, use it for the Rate in remaining calculations.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Inp_Sim)XIO(Cfg_CalcRate)XIO(Wrk_RateInfNaN)MOV(Inp_RatePV,Wrk_Rate);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Totalizer is Running, we're not using the Rate to calculate Quantity, the input is not
simulated, and there is a Rollover value, calculate how much the quantity has
changed since last scan, accounting for the input rolling over its maximum back to zero.
The multiplier for counts per EU must be valid (greater than zero).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_RunTot)XIO(Cfg_CalcQty)XIO(Inp_Sim)GRT(Cfg_Rollover,0.0)[GRT(Cfg_CountsPerEU,0.0) [LES(Inp_QtyPV,Wrk_PrevQty) CPT(Wrk_AmtToAdd,(Cfg_Rollover+Inp_QtyPV-Wrk_PrevQty)/Cfg_CountsPerEU) ,GEQ(Inp_QtyPV,Wrk_PrevQty) CPT(Wrk_AmtToAdd,(Inp_QtyPV-Wrk_PrevQty)/Cfg_CountsPerEU) ] ,LEQ(Cfg_CountsPerEU,0.0) CLR(Wrk_AmtToAdd) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Copy the current input to a "Previous Quantity" rung for use in the
difference calculations (CPTs) in the rung above next scan.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(Inp_QtyPV,Wrk_PrevQty);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the totalizer is running, and we are totalizing (integrating) the Rate to get Quantity,
calculate the amount to totalize this scan based on the rate and scan time.

NOTE: the simulation rates are ALWAYS integrated to get get quantity when running in simulation.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_RunTot)[XIC(Cfg_CalcQty) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) ][LES(Wrk_Rate,Cfg_LoRateCutoff) OTE(Sts_LoRateCutoff) CLR(Wrk_AmtToAdd) ,XIO(Sts_LoRateCutoff) [GRT(Cfg_RateTime,0.0) CPT(Wrk_AmtToAdd,Wrk_Rate/Cfg_RateTime*Wrk_ScanTime*Cfg_EUQtyMult) ,LEQ(Cfg_RateTime,0.0) CLR(Wrk_AmtToAdd) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Now for the cases where we are adding with the totalizer (not just using the quantity input directly),
add the amount this scan to the totalizer.  We use TWO registers: an Integer for the whole
units and a Real for the fractional units.  This lets us accumulate over 2 billion units
while still keeping the five- or six-digits accuracy after the decimal.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(Cfg_Rollover,0.0) ,XIC(Cfg_CalcQty) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) ]XIO(Wrk_QtyInfNaN)[XIC(Wrk_RunTot) [ADD(Wrk_AmtToAdd,Wrk_LoOrderTot,Wrk_LoOrderTot) ,CPT(Wrk_HiOrderTot,Wrk_HiOrderTot+(TRN(Wrk_LoOrderTot))) ,CPT(Wrk_LoOrderTot,Wrk_LoOrderTot-(TRN(Wrk_LoOrderTot))) ] ,ADD(Wrk_LoOrderTot,Wrk_HiOrderTot,Val_Qty) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung handles the case where the Quantity input is used directly, for example, when
the flowmeter has a totalizer on board and we are using its total.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Cfg_CalcQty)XIO(Inp_Sim)LEQ(Cfg_Rollover,0.0)XIO(Wrk_QtyInfNaN)[GRT(Cfg_CountsPerEU,0.0) DIV(Inp_QtyPV,Cfg_CountsPerEU,Val_Qty) ,LEQ(Cfg_CountsPerEU,0.0) MOV(Inp_QtyPV,Val_Qty) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the Rate is to be calculated based on change in quantity, take the change in Quantity
calculated above, divide by scan time, adjust for per second, per minute, per hour (etc.),
and adjust for conversion of quantity units to rate units (e.g. GPM to BBL/Day...).
Then filter (1st order) based on the entered time constant.

If the rate is NOT to be calculated, just pass through the input Rate PV to the Val_Rate.

If the input was +/-Infinity or Not a Number and it becomes a valid number,
initialize the filter to start from the first valid value.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Wrk_RateInfNaN)[XIC(Cfg_CalcRate) [GRT(Wrk_ScanTime,0.0) CPT(Wrk_Rate,Wrk_AmtToAdd/Wrk_ScanTime*Cfg_RateTime) ,LEQ(Wrk_ScanTime,0.0) CLR(Wrk_Rate) ] ,GRT(Cfg_RateFiltTC,0.0) CPT(Wrk_Alpha,1.0/(1.0+Wrk_ScanTime/Cfg_RateFiltTC)) ,LEQ(Cfg_RateFiltTC,0.0) CLR(Wrk_Alpha) ,ONS(Wrk_ValidONS) MOV(Wrk_Rate,Wrk_FiltRate) ,CPT(Wrk_FiltRate,(Wrk_Alpha*Wrk_FiltRate)+((1.0-Wrk_Alpha)*Wrk_Rate)) MOV(Wrk_FiltRate,Val_Rate) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[We have Rate, Quantity and Setpoint all determined above.
Now find the quantity yet to be delivered (Val_Remain).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[SUB(Val_SP,Val_Qty,Val_Remain);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung gives us a Percent Complete value that is between zero and 100%,
and always makes sense based on the Setpoint and actual quantity delivered.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[GRT(Val_SP,0.0) CPT(Wrk_PctComplete,100.0*Val_Qty/Val_SP) ,LEQ(Val_SP,0.0) MOV(100.0,Wrk_PctComplete) ,LES(Wrk_PctComplete,0.0) CLR(Wrk_PctComplete) ,GRT(Wrk_PctComplete,100.0) MOV(100.0,Wrk_PctComplete) ,MOV(Wrk_PctComplete,Val_PctComplete) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="34" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
EQUIPMENT FAULT DETERMINATION
============================================================
If the input being used to calculate the Rate (flow) is BAD, the Rate is BAD (failed).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Inp_QtyPVBad) XIC(Cfg_CalcRate) ,XIC(Inp_RatePVBad) XIO(Cfg_CalcRate) ,XIC(Wrk_RateInfNaN) ]XIO(Inp_Sim)OTE(Sts_RateBad);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="35" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the input being used to calculate the Quantity (total) is UNCERTAIN, the Quantity is UNCERTAIN.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Inp_RatePVUncertain) XIC(Cfg_CalcQty) ,XIC(Inp_QtyPVUncertain) XIO(Cfg_CalcQty) ]XIO(Inp_Sim)OTE(Sts_QtyUncertain);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="36" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the input being used to calculate the Rate (flow) is UNCERTAIN, the Rate is UNCERTAIN.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Inp_RatePVUncertain) XIO(Cfg_CalcRate) ,XIC(Inp_QtyPVUncertain) XIC(Cfg_CalcRate) ]XIO(Inp_Sim)OTE(Sts_RateUncertain);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="37" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If we have equipment feedback and are not running in simulation,
and if the Fault Time is set to a number other than 0,
check the equipment feedback to see if the equipment
is following the output that is commanding it.
If the equipment state doesn't match the output state, run the Fault timer.

#####  V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Modified simulated equipment feedback.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_HasEqpFdbk)XIO(Inp_Sim)GRT(Cfg_FaultT,0)[XIC(Out_StopFlow) NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,1) ,XIC(Out_RunFlow) NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,2) ,XIC(Out_DribbleFlow) NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,3) ]TON(Wrk_FaultT,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="38" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the controlled equipment faults, or if the input being used to control quantity fails,
or if the equipment feedback is being used and the equipment is not going
to the commanded state, show an Equipment Fault (and alarm).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Sts_QtyBad) ,XIC(Inp_CtrldEqpFault) XIO(Inp_Sim) ,XIC(Wrk_FaultT.DN) ]OTE(Sts_EqpFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="39" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
SHED ON FAULT LOGIC
============================================================
This rung handles latching in of conditions which are configured to cause
motor to shed (de-energize).

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_EqpFault)XIC(Cfg_ShedOnEqpFault)OTL(Nrdy_EqpFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="40" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The dosing is NOT READY to be controlled (by the owner specified by Mode) if it has
a bad Quantity input or if the controlled dosing equipment is Faulted.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Nrdy_NoMode)[XIC(Nrdy_EqpFault) ,XIC(Sts_QtyBad) OTE(Nrdy_PVBad) ,XIC(Sts_Err) OTE(Nrdy_CfgErr) ]OTE(Sts_NotRdy);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="41" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The dosing is AVAILABLE to be controlled by other objects
if it IS in Program Mode and it IS NOT "Not Ready".]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Sts_Prog)XIO(Sts_NotRdy)OTE(Sts_Available);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="42" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OUTPUT HANDLING
============================================================
This rung generates the Out_ClearTot signal
to clear an external Totalizer (say, on board a fieldbus flowmeter).

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_ClearTot) ,XIC(Wrk_ClearPulseT.TT) ][TON(Wrk_ClearPulseT,?,?) ,OTE(Out_ClearTot) MOV(1,Wrk_Cmd) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="43" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung clears the internal totalizer used when we only have a rate input.
When the totalizer clear pulse is complete, this rung makes sure the reported total coming
back from the device is zero (or the internal totalizer cleared and did not count up).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_ClearTot)[CLR(Wrk_HiOrderTot) CLR(Wrk_LoOrderTot) ,[XIC(Wrk_ClearPulseT.DN) ,EQU(Val_Qty,0.0) OTU(Wrk_ZeroFault) ] [OTU(Wrk_ClearTot) ,NEQ(Val_Qty,0.0) OTL(Wrk_ZeroFault) ] ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="44" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the totalizer should be running, tell the device, in case we are using a totalizer on board the meter.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_RunTot)OTE(Out_RunTot);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="45" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If flow should be running (and not dribbling), tell the controlled equipment to run.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_RunFlow) [XIC(Cfg_HasDribble) CMP(Val_Qty<(Val_SP-Val_Preact-Val_DribbleQty)) ,XIO(Cfg_HasDribble) CMP(Val_Qty<(Val_SP-Val_Preact)) ] ,XIC(Wrk_BumpFlow) XIO(Cfg_HasDribble) ]XIO(Sts_NotRdy)OTE(Out_RunFlow);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="46" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the flow should be dribbling (on running or bumping), tell the controlled equipment to run at the dribble rate.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_HasDribble)[XIC(Wrk_RunFlow) CMP(Val_Qty>=(Val_SP-Val_Preact-Val_DribbleQty)) CMP(Val_Qty<(Val_SP-Val_Preact)) ,XIC(Wrk_BumpFlow) ]XIO(Sts_NotRdy)OTE(Out_DribbleFlow);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="47" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If not dribbling, not bumping, not flowing, tell the controlled equipment to stop.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIO(Out_RunFlow)XIO(Out_DribbleFlow)OTE(Out_StopFlow);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="48" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The following rungs generate Status bits (not already generated above) for this object.

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Settle Timer  #####
#####  V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Modified simulated equipment feedback.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[EQU(Val_Qty,0.0) OTE(Sts_Cleared) ,XIC(Out_RunTot) OTE(Sts_TotRunning) ,XIC(Out_StopFlow) [EQU(Wrk_Fdbk,1) [OTE(Sts_FlowStopped) ,TON(Wrk_SettleT,?,?) ] ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,1) OTE(Sts_FlowStopping) ] ,XIC(Out_RunFlow) [EQU(Wrk_Fdbk,2) OTE(Sts_FlowRunning) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,2) OTE(Sts_FlowStarting) ] ,XIC(Out_DribbleFlow) [EQU(Wrk_Fdbk,3) OTE(Sts_FlowDribble) ,NEQ(Wrk_Fdbk,3) OTE(Sts_DribbleStarting) ] ,XIC(Wrk_BumpFlow) OTE(Sts_Bumping) ,CMP(Val_Qty>=(Val_SP-Val_Preact)) XIO(Wrk_BumpFlow) OTU(Wrk_RunFlow) OTE(Sts_Complete) ,XIC(Wrk_OverTol) OTE(Sts_OverTol) ,XIC(Wrk_UnderTol) OTE(Sts_UnderTol) ,XIC(Wrk_InTol) OTE(Sts_InTol) ,XIC(Wrk_ZeroFault) OTE(Sts_ZeroFault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="49" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung generates the enumerated Device Status:
0 = PowerUp/Reset
1 = Stopped
2 = Totalizing
3 = Delivering
4 = Dribbling
5 = Bumping
6 = Starting Delivery
7 = Starting Dribble
8 = Stopping
33 = Disabled (here or in EnableInFalse routine)

And this rung generates the enumerated Device Fault Status:
0 = none
17 = Equipment Fault
34 = Configuration Error]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Sts) CLR(Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Sts_FlowStopped) MOV(1,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_TotRunning) MOV(2,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_FlowRunning) MOV(3,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_FlowDribble) MOV(4,Wrk_Sts) ,XIC(Sts_Bumping) MOV(5,Wrk_Sts) MOV(5,Wrk_Cmd) ,XIC(Sts_FlowStarting) MOV(6,Wrk_Sts) MOV(3,Wrk_Cmd) ,XIC(Sts_DribbleStarting) MOV(7,Wrk_Sts) MOV(4,Wrk_Cmd) ,XIC(Sts_FlowStopping) MOV(8,Wrk_Sts) MOV(6,Wrk_Cmd) ,XIC(Sts_EqpFault) MOV(17,Wrk_Fault) ,XIC(Sts_Err) MOV(34,Wrk_Fault) ,MOV(Wrk_Cmd,Val_Cmd) MOV(Wrk_Sts,Val_Sts) MOV(Wrk_Fault,Val_Fault) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="50" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ENUMERATED STATUS VALUES
============================================================
Source and Quality (Srcq) for Val_InpPV
Start with the Srcq from the Input Channel object if it's available.
Otherwise, start based on bad/uncertain input bits.

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Cfg_CalcQty) MOV(Inp_RatePVSrcQ,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIO(Cfg_CalcQty) MOV(Inp_QtyPVSrcQ,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIO(Cfg_HasEqpFdbk) LES(Wrk_SrcQ,2) MOV(2,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Cfg_CalcQty) [XIC(Sts_RateUncertain) MOV(16,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Sts_RateBad) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Wrk_RateInfNaN) MOV(32,Wrk_SrcQ) ] ,XIO(Cfg_CalcQty) [XIC(Sts_QtyUncertain) MOV(16,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Sts_QtyBad) MOV(34,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Wrk_QtyInfNaN) MOV(32,Wrk_SrcQ) ] ,XIC(Err_EU) MOV(35,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Inp_Sim) MOV(10,Wrk_SrcQ) ,MOV(Wrk_SrcQ,SrcQ_IO) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="51" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Source and Quality (SrcQ) for Val (primary value)

0 = Good: live, confirmed good;   1 = Good: live, assumed good;
2 = Good: no feedback, assumed good;   8 = Test: Simulated;   9 = Test: Loopback;
10 = Test: Manually Entered;   16 = Uncertain: Live, off-spec;
17 = Uncertain, Substituted at Device / Bus;   18 = Uncertain, Substituted at AOI;
19 = Uncertain, using last known good;    20 = Uncertain, using replacement value;
32 = Bad, Signal Failure;   33 = Bad, Channel Fault;
34 = Bad, Module / Comms Fault;   35 = Bad, Invalid Configuration

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Added rung for Source/Quality enumerations.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[MOV(SrcQ_IO,Wrk_SrcQ) ,XIC(Cfg_HasEqpFdbk) XIO(Cfg_UseEqpFdbk) LES(Wrk_SrcQ,18) MOV(18,Wrk_SrcQ) ,MOV(SrcQ_IO,SrcQ) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="52" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
OPERATOR COMMAND READIES
============================================================
All commands require Mode to be Operator or Maintenance.

Ready to Clear Total at any time if no flow requested.
Ready to Start Totalizer if not Running and PV not BAD.
Ready to Stop Totalizer if Running.
Ready to Start flow if not flowing, totalizer running and not past Preact.
Ready to Stop flow if flowing or in bump.
Ready to Check Tolerances if PV is not BAD and not flowing.
Ready to bump if PV not BAD, past preact but not complete, totalizer is running, and not flowing.

NOTE:  Keep the BUMP button active as long as a bump is in progress if
the Bump Time is 0 -- this keeps the button on-screen so the bump command is
cleared if the operator releases the button!!!

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Settle Timer  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Sts_Oper) XIO(Cfg_ProgKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Prog) XIC(Cfg_OperKeep.0) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ][XIO(Wrk_RunFlow) XIO(Wrk_BumpFlow) OTE(Rdy_ClearTot) ,XIO(Wrk_RunTot) XIO(Sts_RateBad) XIO(Sts_Err) OTE(Rdy_StartTot) ,XIC(Wrk_RunTot) OTE(Rdy_StopTot) ,XIO(Wrk_RunFlow) XIO(Sts_Complete) XIC(Wrk_RunTot) XIO(Sts_NotRdy) OTE(Rdy_StartFlow) ,[XIC(Wrk_RunFlow) ,XIC(Wrk_BumpFlow) ] OTE(Rdy_StopFlow) ,XIO(Sts_Cleared) XIO(Wrk_RunFlow) XIO(Wrk_BumpFlow) XIO(Sts_QtyBad) XIC(Wrk_SettleT.DN) OTE(Rdy_CheckTol) ,[LES(Val_Qty,Val_SP) XIC(Wrk_RunTot) XIO(Wrk_RunFlow) ,XIC(Wrk_BumpFlow) EQU(Wrk_BumpT.PRE,0) ] XIO(Sts_NotRdy) OTE(Rdy_Bump) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="53" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Ready to receive Operator Setpoint Setting (OSet_SP) if tracking is NOT enabled,
or we're in Operator or Maintenance Mode and Program doesn't KEEP this setting,
of if we're in Program Mode and Program DOES keep this setting.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_SetTrack) ,XIC(Sts_Oper) XIO(Cfg_ProgKeep.1) ,XIC(Sts_Prog) XIC(Cfg_OperKeep.1) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ]OTE(Rdy_SP);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="54" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Ready to receive Operator Dribble and Preact Settings (OSet_DribbleQty, OSet_Preact)
if tracking is NOT enabled, or we're in Operator or Maintenance Mode and Program doesn't
KEEP these settings, of if we're in Program Mode and Program DOES keep these settings.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_SetTrack) ,XIC(Sts_Oper) XIO(Cfg_ProgKeep.2) ,XIC(Sts_Prog) XIC(Cfg_OperKeep.2) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ]OTE(Rdy_DribPre);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="55" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Ready to receive Operator Tolerance Settings (OSet_TolHi, OSet_TolLo)
if tracking is NOT enabled, or we're in Operator or Maintenance Mode and Program doesn't
KEEP these settings, of if we're in Program Mode and Program DOES keep these settings.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(Cfg_SetTrack) ,XIC(Sts_Oper) XIO(Cfg_ProgKeep.3) ,XIC(Sts_Prog) XIC(Cfg_OperKeep.3) ,XIC(Sts_Maint) ]OTE(Rdy_Tol);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="56" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
ALARM PROCESSING
============================================================
Pass the Cfg_PCmdClear configuration down to each P_Alarm instance.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(OverTol.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(UnderTol.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(ZeroFault.Cfg_PCmdClear)OTE(EqpFault.Cfg_PCmdClear);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="57" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The various alarms are ALWAYS allowed to Exist (Cfg_HasXxxAlarm can be 1).

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added PCfg_AllowExist on P_Alarm 3.0.  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTL(OverTol.PCfg_AllowExist)OTL(UnderTol.PCfg_AllowExist)OTL(ZeroFault.PCfg_AllowExist)OTL(EqpFault.PCfg_AllowExist);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="58" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Delivery Over Tolerance Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(OverTol);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="59" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Delivery Under Tolerance Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(UnderTol);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="60" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Zero Fault Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(ZeroFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="61" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Handle Equipment Fault Alarm Processing using the standard P_Alarm AOI.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[P_Alarm(EqpFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="62" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If ANY alarm is Disabled, Inhibited or Suppressed, set the Alarm Inhibit
summary status bit (which puts the "I" box on the graphic symbol).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(OverTol.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(UnderTol.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(ZeroFault.Sts_AlmInh) ,XIC(EqpFault.Sts_AlmInh) ]OTE(Sts_AlmInh);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="63" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
NOTIFICATION VALUE
============================================================
Indicate the current alarm notification level as the max of any of the alarms,
and set the low-order bit for reset or ack required:
0 = Not in alarm, acknowledged
1 = Not in alarm, unacknowledged or reset required
2 = Low severity alarm, acknowledged
3 = Low severity alarm, unacknowledged
4 = Medium severity alarm, acknowledged
5 = Medium severity alarm, unacknowledged
6 = High severity alarm, acknowledged
7 = High severity alarm, unacknowledged
8 = Urgent severity alarm, acknowledged
9 = Urgent severity alarm, unacknowledged

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Separated Reset Reqd functions from Val_Notify  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[CLR(Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(OverTol.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(OverTol.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(UnderTol.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(UnderTol.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(ZeroFault.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(ZeroFault.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,GRT(EqpFault.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) MOV(EqpFault.Val_Notify,Wrk_Notify) ,[XIC(OverTol.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(UnderTol.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(ZeroFault.Val_Notify.0) ,XIC(EqpFault.Val_Notify.0) ] OTE(Wrk_Notify.0) ,MOV(Wrk_Notify,Val_Notify) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="64" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung identifies:
* if a latched Shed condition requires a reset in order to run the motor;
* if that reset or any alarm reset or other reset is required; and
* if any reset or acknowledge from the operator is required.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx); split from Val_Notify logic (above).  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[[XIC(OverTol.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(UnderTol.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(ZeroFault.Rdy_Ack) ,XIC(EqpFault.Rdy_Ack) ] ,[XIC(OverTol.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(UnderTol.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(ZeroFault.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(EqpFault.Rdy_Reset) ,XIC(Nrdy_EqpFault) XIO(Sts_EqpFault) ] OTE(Rdy_Reset) ]OTE(Rdy_ResetAckAll);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Prescan" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Clear Ownership, clear "lurking" Commands, all Readies]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
PRESCAN (POWERUP) HANDLING
============================================================
On Prescan, set the Ownership to NO OWNER (0).]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(PSet_Owner)CLR(Val_Owner);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Program Commands are cleared if they are set as "Edge" triggered
(cleared by this object as received).
(Lurking Acknowledge Commands are left to perform their action.)

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added PCmd_Bump  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Cfg_PCmdClear)[OTU(PCmd_StartTot) OTU(PCmd_StopTot) OTU(PCmd_StartFlow) OTU(PCmd_StopFlow) ,OTU(PCmd_Bump) OTU(PCmd_ClearTot) OTU(PCmd_CheckTol) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA["Lurking" Operator Commands are cleared, as well as Program Reset.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(OCmd_StartTot) OTU(OCmd_StopTot) OTU(OCmd_StartFlow) OTU(OCmd_StopFlow) OTU(OCmd_ClearTot) ,OTU(OCmd_CheckTol) OTU(OCmd_Bump) OTU(OCmd_Reset) OTU(OCmd_ResetAckAll) OTU(PCmd_Reset) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[The Dosing "run" and latched fault stored latches are cleared on Prescan.
The logic should come up with the totalizer and flow "Stopped".
After Powerup, a "Check Tolerance" should NOT do a preact adjustment (invalid data)!

#####  V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Settle Timer  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[OTU(Wrk_ClearTot) OTU(Wrk_RunTot) OTU(Wrk_RunFlow) OTU(Wrk_BumpFlow) ,OTL(Wrk_BumpNoAdj) RES(Wrk_BumpT) RES(Wrk_SettleT) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Clear shed latches on powerup.

#####  V3.1-00  2014-06-30: Added Not Ready reason bits (Nrdy_xxx)  #####]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Nrdy_EqpFault);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Set up the filter initialization one-shot so filter will start from first valid value.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Wrk_ValidONS);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[All Outputs are de-energized on Prescan.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Out_RunFlow)OTU(Out_DribbleFlow)OTU(Out_StopFlow);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[On Prescan, clear the following:
Val_Cmd (no command active)
Val_Fdbk (device position not determined)
Val_Sts (device status powerup / unknown)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CLR(Val_Cmd)CLR(Val_Fdbk)CLR(Val_Sts);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
<Dependencies>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_40"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_20"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_8"/>
<Dependency Type="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="P_Alarm"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_12"/>
<Dependency Type="DataType" Name="STRING_16"/>
<Dependency Type="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="P_Mode"/>
</Dependencies>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
